# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Written by a failing `toMatchScreenshot()` (actual/diff images for local
# review). The committed baseline lives in __screenshots__/ instead.
.vitest-attachments/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea

# The engine submodule builds its own dist/ under engine/src/engine/dist —
# already covered by the bare dist/ pattern above, since git applies .gitignore
# recursively. The engine repo's own .gitignore governs everything else inside
# the submodule; this file only governs paths git tracks as part of this repo.

# npm pack output
*.tgz
# ...except a genuinely vendored package (server/vendor/ -- CLAUDE.md, "Nothing checks that
# the server still matches the engine's contract"). The bare pattern above would otherwise
# swallow it, and a vendored artifact that silently never gets committed defeats the point
# of vendoring it.
!server/vendor/*.tgz

# Env / secrets
.env
# Also covers `.env.preview` (scripts/deploy-preview.mjs's configuration, docs/preview.md),
# which names a host you can SSH into and so is never committed. Its variables are
# documented in docs/preview.md rather than in a `.env.preview.example`, which the pattern
# below would swallow anyway -- the `!` exception is for that one exact filename.
.env.*
# ...except the committed template. `.env.*` above would otherwise swallow it, and a
# .env.example that silently never gets committed is worse than none at all.
!.env.example
*.local

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
